hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1633","Narrated to us Muḥammad ibn Bashshār: narrated to us Yaḥyā: on the authority of Ibn ʿAjlān: from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Miqsam: from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh (RA) who said:\n*\"Muʿādh ibn Jabal (RA) would pray with the Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ), then return and lead his people in prayer, and he would pray that same prayer with them.\"*\n\n**CHAPTER:**"
"1634","Narrated to us Yaḥyā ibn Ḥabīb al-Ḥārithee, narrated to us Khālid (meaning ibn al-Ḥārith), on the authority of Muḥammad ibn ʿAjlān, on the authority of ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Miqsam, on the authority of Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh (RA), who said:\n\nMuʿādh (RA) used to pray the ʿIshāʾ prayer with the Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ), then he would return and lead his companions in prayer. One day, he returned and led them in prayer, and a young man from his people prayed behind him. When the prayer became long for the young man, he prayed on his own and left. He took hold of his camel’s halter and they departed.\n\nWhen Muʿādh (RA) finished the prayer, this was mentioned to him, so he said, “Verily this is hypocrisy! I must inform the Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) about it.” So Muʿādh (RA) informed him of what the young man had done.\n\nThe young man said, “O Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ)! He lingers so long with you, then returns and prolongs the prayer for us.”\n\nThe Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) said, “Are you causing division, O Muʿādh?” Then he said to the young man, “How do you pray, O nephew?”\n\nHe said, “I recite the Opening of the Book (Sūrah al-Fātiḥah), ask Allāh for Paradise, and seek refuge with Him from the Fire. And I do not know what your murmuring and Muʿādh’s murmuring is.”\n\nThe Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) said, “Indeed, I and Muʿādh are around these two,” or something to that effect.\n\nThe young man said, “But Muʿādh will soon know when the people arrive and have been informed that the enemy has drawn near.”\n\nHe said, “So they arrived, and the young man was martyred.”\n\nAfter that, the Prophet (ﷺ) said to Muʿādh (RA), “What has become of my opponent and your opponent?”\n\nHe said, “O Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ)! He spoke the truth and I lied. He was martyred.”\n\n---\n\n**CHAPTER:**"
